{
  "data": {
    "title": "A Brain-Wide Study of Age-Related Changes in Functional Connectivity",
    "text": "Title: A Brain-Wide Study of Age-Related Changes in Functional Connectivity\n\nFunctional connectivity analysis\nWhole-brain functional connectivity was assessed using Pearson correlation coefficients between regional mean BOLD time series. Regions of interest were defined using a whole-brain parcellation, and correlation matrices were constructed for each participant.\n\nGraph-theoretical analysis\nConnectivity matrices were analyzed using graph-theoretical approaches. Weighted undirected graphs were constructed, and graph measures including global efficiency, local efficiency, clustering coefficient, and degree were calculated. Analyses were performed across a range of connection densities, and graph metrics were averaged across thresholds."
